  "function_code": 31,
  "name": "Test Quality",
  "description": "The test quality function code checks the point quality of up to four inputs. It is a four input logical OR function that sets the output to a logic 0 if all tested points are good, and to a logic 1 if one or more tested inputs are bad. Analog and digital I/O and Cnet inputs can be tested for quality. Quality is not propagated through module function blocks. All internal points will have good quality.",
  "description_lines": [
